<section id="medicines" class="panel active"><div class="section"><div class="ey">THE COMPARATIVE CHART</div><h2>Every medicine against the same required body result</h2><p class="lead">Read across the row: desired effect → how the medicine creates it → collateral path → ILMB route → proof. ILMB does not claim molecular equivalence unless it is demonstrated.</p><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare"><thead><tr><th>Medicine</th><th>Desired effect</th><th>How it achieves it</th><th>Important collateral / side-effect path</th><th>ILMB target</th><th>Actual ILMB route</th><th>What proves the result</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Clopidogrel 75 mg<small>Clopilet</small></td><td>Platelet aggregation ↓</td><td>P2Y12 inhibition → ADP signalling ↓</td><td class="harm">Bleeding/bruising can increase because normal hemostasis is also reduced; rare TTP is reported.</td><td class="ilmb">Reduce the non-platelet contributors to net thrombosis risk.</td><td>Current medicine unchanged → quantify MCA flow/collaterals/perfusion + BP + TG/non-HDL/apoB + CBC/platelets → reduce measured vascular/metabolic contributors → remeasure. <span class="status">SUPPORTIVE · NOT A P2Y12 SUBSTITUTE</span></td><td>Recurrence/bleeding context; CBC/platelets; vascular state; lipid/metabolic outputs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Aspirin 150 mg<small>Ecosprin</small></td><td>TXA₂-mediated platelet aggregation ↓</td><td>COX-1 inhibition → thromboxane ↓</td><td class="harm">Platelet hemostasis ↓; GI irritation/bleeding risk.</td><td class="ilmb">Reduce net thrombotic pressure through alternate measurable routes.</td><td>Medicine unchanged → quantify bleeding/GI burden + BP + vascular state + metabolic state → correct measurable contributors → remeasure. <span class="status">SUPPORTIVE · NOT COX-1 EQUIVALENCE</span></td><td>Bleeding/GI symptoms; CBC/platelets; recurrence; vascular outputs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Amlodipine 5 mg</td><td>BP / vascular resistance ↓</td><td>L-type Ca²⁺ blockade → arterial relaxation</td><td class="harm">Edema, dizziness and hypotension can occur.</td><td class="ilmb">Lower BP through measured non-drug contributors.</td><td>7-day BP/pulse baseline → quantify sodium/fluid input, sleep, activity/autonomic state → change one abnormal contributor → repeat 7-day mean. <span class="status">DIRECTLY MEASURABLE</span></td><td>Mean SBP/DBP, pulse, edema/dizziness and repeat response.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Atenolol 50 mg</td><td>HR and cardiac workload ↓</td><td>β1 blockade</td><td class="harm">Bradycardia, hypotension, fatigue/dizziness; exercise HR response suppressed.</td><td class="ilmb">Lower resting demand through conditioning/autonomic route.</td><td>Resting HR/BP + fatigue + workload baseline → quantify functional capacity and perceived exertion → carefully dose conditioning from measured capacity → repeat same workload test. <span class="status">FUNCTIONAL ROUTE</span></td><td>Resting HR/BP, RPE, fatigue/dizziness, functional workload.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Atorvastatin 40 mg<small>Lipvas 40</small></td><td>LDL / apoB ↓</td><td>HMG-CoA reductase inhibition → LDL clearance ↑</td><td class="harm">Myopathy and liver-enzyme abnormalities can occur; rare rhabdomyolysis documented.</td><td class="ilmb">Lower atherogenic particle burden through measured substrate/metabolic routes.</td><td>Verify fasting LDL/non-HDL/apoB + 3 weighed food days → convert grams to composition/chemistry → alter one verified substrate route → remeasure lipids. <span class="status">FUNCTIONAL · NOT HMG-CoA EQUIVALENCE</span></td><td>LDL-C, non-HDL-C, apoB, TG, ALT/AST, muscle symptoms.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fenofibrate 160 mg</td><td>TG-rich particles ↓</td><td>PPARα activation → TG clearance ↑</td><td class="harm">Liver injury/enzyme rise, muscle injury, reversible creatinine rise, gallstones; statin combination raises muscle risk.</td><td class="ilmb">Reduce hepatic TG substrate and increase measured utilisation.</td><td>3 weighed food days → IFCT/USDA composition → ChEBI chemical inputs + measured movement baseline → change one verified substrate/activity input → repeat fasting TG. <span class="status">DIRECTLY MEASURABLE</span></td><td>Fasting TG, ALT/AST/GGT, creatinine/eGFR, movement dose, muscle symptoms.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Cod liver oil 300 mg</td><td>Nutrient exposure</td><td>Depends on actual EPA/DHA/vitamin A/vitamin D chemistry</td><td class="harm">Dose-dependent excess and interaction burden are possible.</td><td class="ilmb">Requirement-first chemical dosing.</td><td>Read exact label → quantify EPA/DHA/A/D → compare against measured need and concurrent intake → decide whether input is useful, redundant or excessive. <span class="status">BLOCKED UNTIL LABEL VERIFIED</span></td><td>Exact label chemistry and relevant biomarkers.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Neurobion Forte</td><td>B-vitamin cofactor support</td><td>Multiple B-vitamin cofactors</td><td class="harm">Formulation and dose matter; excess is not automatically beneficial.</td><td class="ilmb">Nutrient-by-nutrient requirement calculation.</td><td>Read exact formulation → map each nutrient to chemistry → compare with food intake and need-specific markers → retain only justified inputs. <span class="status">BLOCKED UNTIL FORMULATION VERIFIED</span></td><td>B12 and need-specific markers where relevant.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><div class="call"><b>Boundary:</b> Nilesh does not stop or reduce prescribed medicines because an ILMB route exists. ILMB first measures whether an alternate route changes the required physiological output safely and reproducibly.</div></div></section>
<section id="path" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">MY ILMB PATH · ACTUAL METHOD</div><h2>What Nilesh does, what changes, and what number decides the next step</h2><p class="lead">Each route is classified. Unknowns stay unknown. The first intervention is released only after baseline inputs are verified.</p><div class="paths">
<details class="path" open><summary><b>01</b><strong>Prevent another ischemic event</strong><span>Platelet/thrombosis protection</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Route</b><p>Reduce non-platelet contributors: vascular pressure, endothelial stress, triglyceride-rich particles, inactivity and unresolved metabolic load.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Action now</b><p>Keep aspirin/clopidogrel unchanged. Record bleeding/bruising. Obtain current CBC/platelets and resolve current MCA flow/collaterals/perfusion.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Measure</b><p>CBC/platelets, BP, TG/non-HDL/apoB, vascular imaging/perfusion question, recurrent neurologic symptoms.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>No replacement claim without demonstrated recurrence protection.</p><span class="status">SUPPORTIVE ONLY</span></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>02</b><strong>Lower blood pressure / vascular resistance</strong><span>Amlodipine + atenolol body goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Route</b><p>Autonomic state, sodium/fluid input, sleep, conditioning and endothelial load.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Action now</b><p>7 days: morning + evening; seated 5 min; 2 BP readings 1 min apart. Record pulse, dizziness and ankle swelling.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Measure</b><p>7-day mean SBP/DBP/pulse; symptoms; weighed sodium intake; sleep and movement.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>Change one measured contributor and compare the next 7-day mean with baseline.</p><span class="status">DIRECTLY MEASURABLE</span></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>03</b><strong>Reduce triglyceride-rich particles</strong><span>Fenofibrate body goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Route</b><p>Reduce hepatic TG substrate and increase muscle fatty-acid utilisation using measured chemistry and movement.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Action now</b><p>3 normal weighed food/drink/supplement days. Grams → IFCT/USDA → chemical input. Capture movement minutes/workload.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Measure</b><p>Fasting TG, non-HDL, apoB if available, ALT/AST/GGT, weight/waist and movement workload.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>Hold one intervention steady, remeasure fasting TG, calculate Nilesh’s own ΔTG/Δinput.</p><span class="status">DIRECTLY MEASURABLE</span></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>04</b><strong>Lower atherogenic lipid burden</strong><span>Atorvastatin body goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Route</b><p>Intestinal/substrate pattern, hepatic substrate supply, body composition and activity.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Action now</b><p>Verify current fasting lipid method. Use the same weighed food chemistry record so the input is numeric rather than descriptive.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Measure</b><p>LDL-C, non-HDL-C, apoB, TG, ALT/AST and muscle symptoms.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>Track output change; do not label it HMG-CoA equivalence.</p><span class="status">FUNCTIONAL ROUTE</span></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>05</b><strong>Protect brain function and recovery</strong><span>Perfusion + motor network goal</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Route</b><p>Resolve collateral/perfusion state and use task-specific rehabilitation only where a measurable deficit/reserve limitation exists.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Action now</b><p>Baseline bilateral grip, arm/leg strength, 10-m walk, 5× sit-to-stand, dexterity, balance, ROM and tone.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Measure</b><p>Repeat the same test/protocol after a defined rehab block; record fatigue and perceived exertion because atenolol suppresses HR response.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>KEEP if improving; MODIFY if flat; INVESTIGATE if worsening/new neurologic symptoms.</p><span class="status">DIRECTLY MEASURABLE</span></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>06</b><strong>Correct measured nutrient/endocrine deficits safely</strong><span>Vitamin D 13.9 · TSH 5.386</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Route</b><p>Requirement-first correction using exact chemical/formulation identity and current kidney/liver context.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Action now</b><p>Repeat 25-OH-D and TSH with free T4; verify exact cod-liver-oil and Neurobion labels before generating any dose.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Measure</b><p>25-OH-D, contextual mineral markers when relevant, TSH/free T4, B12/need-specific markers, creatinine/eGFR.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>No automatic supplement dose until identity + amount + safety context are resolved.</p><span class="status">BLOCKED UNTIL VERIFIED</span></div></div></details>
<details class="path"><summary><b>07</b><strong>Reduce treatment collateral burden</strong><span>ALT 81 · platelets 133k · eGFR 72</span></summary><div class="path-body"><div class="cell"><b>Route</b><p>Separate disease burden from treatment burden and trend the organs carrying treatment cost.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Action now</b><p>Repeat CBC/platelets, ALT/AST/GGT, creatinine/eGFR; document muscle symptoms, bruising/bleeding, GI symptoms, edema/dizziness and fatigue.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Measure</b><p>Trend every safety marker against both medicine and ILMB intervention timelines.</p></div><div class="cell"><b>Decision</b><p>Safety deterioration triggers clinician review; ILMB does not suppress a side-effect signal.</p><span class="status">SAFETY GATE</span></div></div></details>
</div><div class="now"><h3>What Nilesh does first</h3><ol><li><b>Do not change medicines.</b> Measure around them first.</li><li>Complete the <b>7-day BP + pulse block</b>.</li><li>Complete <b>3 weighed food days</b> so grams become chemical inputs.</li><li>Repeat fasting lipids, CBC/platelets, liver enzymes, creatinine/eGFR, potassium, TSH/free T4 and 25-OH-D.</li><li>Capture the motor baseline with repeatable tests.</li><li>Resolve current right-MCA flow, collateral supply and perfusion.</li><li>Then change one measurable ILMB input, hold it steady, and remeasure the exact output.</li></ol></div><div class="equation">ILMB RESPONSE = (FOLLOW-UP OUTPUT − BASELINE OUTPUT) / VERIFIED CHANGE IN INPUT<br>DECISION = KEEP · MODIFY · INVESTIGATE · ESCALATE</div></div></section>
<section id="reports" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">MY REPORTS</div><h2>What is reassuring, what persists, what is still unknown</h2><div class="timeline"><div class="event"><div><b>23 Aug 2024</b><p>MRI brain</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Multiple fresh non-haemorrhagic right fronto-parieto-temporal infarcts.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Several right-brain regions were injured because blood supply failed.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>23 Aug 2024</b><p>MRA</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>High-grade right MCA occlusion from origin; severe distal paucity.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Main arterial route to a large right-brain territory was severely compromised.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>21 Jul 2025</b><p>MRI/MRA</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Right MCA M1 no flow; faint M2 enhancement possibly collateral.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Vessel abnormality persisted; collateral supply may exist but was not quantified.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>26 Jul 2025</b><p>Clinical follow-up</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Normal speech; no recorded deficit.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Function recovered more than vessel imaging alone suggests—important evidence of compensation/neuroplasticity.</p></div></div><div class="event"><div><b>31 Jul 2026</b><p>Plain CT</p></div><div><strong>Finding</strong><p>Old right-sided infarcts; no acute infarct, haemorrhage or mass.</p></div><div><strong>Meaning</strong><p>Reassuring for no new acute lesion; current MCA lumen/collateral reserve/perfusion still unresolved.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="numbers" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">WHAT WE MEASURE</div><h2>Known values + unresolved outputs</h2><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><small>Triglycerides</small><strong>301 mg/dL</strong><small>LOINC 2571-8</small></div><div class="metric"><small>ALT</small><strong>81 U/L</strong><small>LOINC 1742-6</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Creatinine</small><strong>1.27 mg/dL</strong><small>LOINC 2160-0</small></div><div class="metric"><small>eGFR</small><strong>72</strong><small>Kidney context</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Potassium</small><strong>5.3 mmol/L</strong><small>LOINC 2823-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>Platelets</small><strong>133 ×10³/µL</strong><small>LOINC 777-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>25-OH Vitamin D</small><strong>13.9 ng/mL</strong><small>LOINC 62292-8</small></div><div class="metric"><small>TSH</small><strong>5.386</strong><small>LOINC 3016-3</small></div><div class="metric"><small>HbA1c</small><strong>5.8%</strong><small>LOINC 4548-4</small></div></div><div class="call"><b>Still missing:</b> current right-MCA flow/perfusion/collaterals, quantitative motor baseline, current repeat fasting labs and exact cod-liver-oil/Neurobion chemistry.</div></div></section>
<section id="science" class="panel"><div class="section"><div class="ey">BACKGROUND SCIENCE</div><h2>LOINC, ChEBI and Reactome stay behind the patient story</h2><p class="lead">The patient sees plain English. The database uses exact identities to prevent ambiguous tests, nutrients or pathway claims.</p><div class="flow"><span class="node">Patient result</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">LOINC</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Body state</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">ChEBI</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Reactome</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">ILMB input</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="node">Re-measure</span></div><div class="identity"><span>LOINC 2571-8 · triglycerides</span><span>LOINC 4548-4 · HbA1c</span><span>LOINC 1742-6 · ALT</span><span>LOINC 777-3 · platelets</span><span>ChEBI 16480 · nitric oxide</span><span>ChEBI 15843 · arachidonic acid</span><span>ChEBI 17968 · butyrate</span><span>ChEBI 16828 · L-tryptophan</span></div><div class="call"><b>Governance:</b> unknown is never converted to zero; an unverified mapping never becomes a treatment equation; a supportive ILMB route is never labelled a direct drug substitute.</div></div></section>
</div></main><script>const bs=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-panel]')],ps=[...document.querySelectorAll('.panel')];function show(id){bs.forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('active',b.dataset.panel===id));ps.forEach(p=>p.classList.toggle('active',p.id===id));history.replaceState(null,'','#'+id)}bs.forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>show(b.dataset.panel));const h=location.hash.slice(1);if(document.getElementById(h))show(h);</script></body></html>